{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Joseph saw to Ephraim children of the third generation.</b> Joseph saw to Ephraim children of the fourth generation, and to Manasseh he saw children of the third generation, for the word <b>בני</b> is adjacent to <b>שלשים</b> (i.e., the phrase בני שלשים means 'children of the third [generation]'). The intention is that he saw from the seed of Ephraim children of the fourth generation, and Joseph had in his lifetime a hint of this from his father's blessing — that Ephraim would become a great and mighty nation more than Manasseh; that is what is said (Genesis 48:19): ״גם הוא יהיה לעם וגם הוא יגדל ואולם אחיו הקטן יגדל ממנו״, and the word גם indicates that all the children — the children of Ephraim and the children of Manasseh — all grew up in Joseph's house. But out of Joseph's love for Manasseh the firstborn, he attributed his many children to Joseph, and therefore it is said of them <b>were born upon Joseph's knees.</b> And the reason he needed to mention the children of Machir — who is Gilead son of Machir son of Manasseh, the grandfathers of the daughters of Zelophehad — was to show that Joseph the righteous reared in his house righteous ones, from whom came the daughters of Zelophehad, who were the wise and righteous women of the generation."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:06.882035720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}